-- 2026-09-17 - add the 739 locos in the official IR database that we do not hold
--
-- SOURCE: the official Indian Railway electric loco database, exported
-- 2026-09-17 (loco_17-09), compared against a prod export of div_locos taken
-- the same morning.
--
-- WHY IT MATTERS THAT THESE ARE MOSTLY OTHER RAILWAYS' LOCOS
-- Only about a tenth of div_locos is CR, and that is correct: foreign locos
-- work BB trains constantly (of the locos seen on our sheets, 293 are CR and
-- more than 880 are not). home_shed is what the mis-link check compares
-- against, and hotel_load_oem is what the HOG check reads. A loco with no row
-- here is not a gap in a reference list - it is two checks quietly not running.
--
-- CONVERSIONS APPLIED
--   - DOC "30-Jun-26" becomes 2026-06-30. The two-digit year pivots on the
--     current year: 00-26 is 2000s, 27-99 is 1900s. Verified before writing -
--     no date lands in the future, and the span is 1999 to 2026.
--   - Hotel load: blank, or a word meaning "not fitted", is stored as NULL.
--     Any text there reads as HOG-CAPABLE (is_hog = column is non-empty).
--   - Maker names folded onto the spellings already in the table (SIEMENS to
--     Siemens, MEDHA to Medha) so the column does not gain case variants.
--   - Zone codes upper-cased to match the table (the sheet mixes ECoR/ECOR).
--   - traction_type is Electric for all: the source is the electric loco
--     database, and that includes the WAG12B and D9 partner fleets.
--
-- Purely additive. INSERT IGNORE, so a re-run - or a loco an LPC registers in
-- the meantime - is a no-op rather than an error.

-- Step 1 - how many do we already hold? Expect 0 before the first run.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS already_present FROM div_locos WHERE entered_by = 'ir-sheet-2026-09-17';
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_before FROM div_locos;

-- Step 2 - insert.
INSERT IGNORE INTO div_locos
  (loco_number, loco_type, traction_type, railway_zone, home_shed, status,
   commission_date, traction_converter, hotel_load_oem, data_source, entered_by)
